1
00:00:03,810 --> 00:00:08,450
I am searching for my missing sister.

2
00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:14,410
Shiharu Nanase does not exist.

3
00:00:17,870 --> 00:00:19,380
Why?

4
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:23,710
Why did she die?

5
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:27,370
- Tell me, please!
- Calm down!

6
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:35,370
According to our findings,

7
00:00:35,370 --> 00:00:37,960
you never had a younger sister.

8
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,380
What?

9
00:00:41,030 --> 00:00:43,390
She never existed in the first place.

10
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:48,800
<i>Some people are just made to never exist.</i>

11
00:00:51,330 --> 00:00:53,510
What are you talking about?

12
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:02,150
Nanase.

13
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:06,920
You have been talking about
someone who doesn't exist.

14
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:09,780
That's impossible.

15
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:14,810
Shiharu and I were always together.

16
00:01:15,690 --> 00:01:18,300
So you won't come join me in Tokyo.

17
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:21,950
You'll instead stay here,

18
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:34,950
with Shiharu?

19
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:50,040
That's impossible.

20
00:01:53,570 --> 00:01:56,040
<i>You'll instead stay here,</i>

21
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:10,010
with Shiharu?

22
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:12,540
Impossible.

23
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:18,160
That's impossible!

24
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:10,050
What's up?

25
00:03:12,250 --> 00:03:14,600
I had a terrible dream.

26
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,050
Tell me about it.

27
00:03:17,310 --> 00:03:19,790
In my dream, I disappeared.

28
00:03:21,790 --> 00:03:25,750
It was as if I never existed.

29
00:03:26,650 --> 00:03:29,590
No one even remembered my name.

30
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:33,580
Don't worry.

31
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:36,370
I won't ever forget you.

32
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:53,840
[A sister who never existed]
[Conflicting memories and speculations]

33
00:03:56,070 --> 00:04:00,360
[log.5]

34
00:04:00,850 --> 00:04:02,700
You're free to go.

35
00:04:38,150 --> 00:04:42,270
I spoke with Dr. Furukawa.

36
00:04:42,270 --> 00:04:45,060
We agreed there were misunderstandings,

37
00:04:45,060 --> 00:04:48,070
and she graciously took back her charges.

38
00:04:48,070 --> 00:04:51,350
She will remain your primary psychiatrist.

39
00:04:51,350 --> 00:04:54,000
As if I'd go see her again.

40
00:04:56,070 --> 00:04:58,470
I have no daughter.

41
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:02,230
Then why the funeral?

42
00:05:02,230 --> 00:05:04,560
It was to help end your delusions.

43
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,210
Quit pulling my leg.

44
00:05:06,210 --> 00:05:08,080
I will say it again.

45
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:10,910
I have no daughter.

46
00:05:10,910 --> 00:05:12,540
Impossible.

47
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:16,800
How could I believe that?

48
00:05:20,850 --> 00:05:22,580
Haruka.

49
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:28,020
I know you had a complicated relationship
with your mother.

50
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:31,370
Even though you only had each other.

51
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,730
How is this relevant?

52
00:05:33,730 --> 00:05:35,710
Your mother once told me

53
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:40,550
she'd never seen you earnestly smile before.

54
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:59,290
But after our remarriage,
you slowly began to change.

55
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:05,040
You believed you had a younger sister.

56
00:06:06,310 --> 00:06:10,130
She brought a smile to your face.

57
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:15,060
And we couldn't deny you
your one source of happiness.

58
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:17,960
So...

59
00:06:20,870 --> 00:06:23,010
For years...

60
00:06:24,310 --> 00:06:26,100
And years...

61
00:06:28,270 --> 00:06:31,110
I was merely living a dream?

62
00:06:31,110 --> 00:06:33,450
You created your ideal "family"

63
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:37,830
in order to protect your own heart.

64
00:06:41,690 --> 00:06:47,480
Your mother told me you always had
quite the active imagination.

65
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:50,500
Like that monster you saw
when you were younger.

66
00:06:51,650 --> 00:06:55,870
<i>Do you know what an "imaginary friend" is?</i>

67
00:06:55,870 --> 00:06:59,740
<i>It's a being that exists in your own mind.</i>

68
00:06:59,740 --> 00:07:01,940
<i>Although it's a phenomenon
often seen in children,</i>

69
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:06,500
<i>some adults will "grow"
with these imaginary friends.</i>

70
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:13,540
When you first raised a fuss
about your sister disappearing in the flood,

71
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:19,010
I was relieved.

72
00:07:19,010 --> 00:07:23,400
I assumed you were
growing out of your fantasies.

73
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:28,120
I thought you finally decided
to focus on reality.

74
00:07:29,570 --> 00:07:31,590
No...

75
00:07:31,590 --> 00:07:34,020
Dr. Furukawa also gave me her diagnosis.

76
00:07:34,020 --> 00:07:39,370
She said you were trying to
redo your mother's funeral.

77
00:07:40,210 --> 00:07:43,640
That you regret
how you handled her death.

78
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:45,070
[Dear Haruka]

79
00:07:53,870 --> 00:07:55,580
Haruka?

80
00:08:01,070 --> 00:08:03,130
I don't believe it.

81
00:08:03,130 --> 00:08:06,200
Professor Ishimizaki also knew about Shiharu.

82
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:09,100
I told him to entertain your fantasies.

83
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:14,060
Shiharu's DNA matched those bones.
The Professor was leaving me a message.

84
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:16,730
Even if that were true,

85
00:08:16,730 --> 00:08:20,040
only Ishimizaki would know
the answer to that riddle.

86
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,680
Ishimizaki, who is now also gone.

87
00:08:25,150 --> 00:08:27,870
You have to move on, Haruka.

88
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:38,950
I want you to treasure yourself.

89
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:46,950
How are the investigations going?

90
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:50,250
Well enough, I'd say.

91
00:08:51,230 --> 00:08:53,230
I see.

92
00:08:53,230 --> 00:08:56,170
You do not doubt my son, do you?

93
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:00,430
We're looking into the case from all angles.

94
00:09:13,700 --> 00:09:16,700
Let's leave Ishimizaki's case to the police.

95
00:09:22,330 --> 00:09:24,230
Won't you come to my place?

96
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:26,410
I'd like to be alone.

97
00:09:27,690 --> 00:09:30,440
I won't force you to attend therapy anymore.

98
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:34,550
Just please, continue to take your medicine.

99
00:09:38,250 --> 00:09:39,800
Haruka.

100
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:48,220
I think of you like my real son.

101
00:09:48,770 --> 00:09:51,090
If nothing else, trust me on this.

102
00:10:04,310 --> 00:10:06,400
Hey there, Tada.

103
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:09,270
Got any new leads?

104
00:10:09,270 --> 00:10:12,890
That was Kyoichi Nanase, right?
The head of Nichie Pharmaceutical.

105
00:10:12,890 --> 00:10:14,790
Yeah. He just came to get his son.

106
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:18,370
- Tada.
- His son? Something happened to him?

107
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:23,410
- Mayuzumi, let's go.
- Hold on, Tada.

108
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:26,480
You remember Onodera, yeah?

109
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:31,000
Don't you wanna know what he was chasing
before he was killed?

110
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,020
You got something?

111
00:10:33,020 --> 00:10:35,510
Tell me about Nanase's son.

112
00:10:40,110 --> 00:10:41,910
I'm taking a smoke.

113
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:47,600
Nanase's son was ambushed?

114
00:10:47,600 --> 00:10:48,770
Why?

115
00:10:48,770 --> 00:10:51,060
Beats me.

116
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:55,350
How is Kyoichi Nanase's son
involved in this case?

117
00:10:55,350 --> 00:11:00,520
He found Ishimizaki's body.
He worked in his lab, too.

118
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:04,390
The lab where the bones were stolen from?

119
00:11:04,390 --> 00:11:07,290
The bones from... where was it...

120
00:11:07,290 --> 00:11:10,080
Roopkund.

121
00:11:12,060 --> 00:11:16,560
Nanase's son is at the center of this case.

122
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:19,920
Yeah, well, he was just looking for someone.

123
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:21,120
Who?

124
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:23,670
An imaginary sister.

125
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:31,760
<i>We were all at the whims
of a delusional grad student.</i>

126
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:36,810
Including the poor girl
who was roped into the search.

127
00:11:36,810 --> 00:11:38,190
He had someone helping him?

128
00:11:38,190 --> 00:11:40,150
Yeah, Ishimizaki's niece.

129
00:11:40,150 --> 00:11:43,350
I don't know much about her, though.

130
00:11:43,350 --> 00:11:44,620
Surely you know something.

131
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:47,400
That's enough from me for now.

132
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:49,370
Tell me what you know.

133
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:52,190
Fair enough.

134
00:11:52,190 --> 00:11:56,250
And you'd better tell me everything.

135
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:06,270
It's all tied to the Plantae.

136
00:12:06,270 --> 00:12:08,790
- Damn it...
- What?

137
00:12:08,790 --> 00:12:13,110
They've got political connections,
and ties to our higher-ups.

138
00:12:13,110 --> 00:12:17,550
You'd better not be bluffing.
They're a hard target for us.

139
00:12:17,550 --> 00:12:19,810
I'm still looking into
the specifics of it all.

140
00:12:19,810 --> 00:12:23,720
But I'm certain the Nichie President
and Plantae are connected somehow.

141
00:12:24,270 --> 00:12:27,890
I've even got a photo to prove it.

142
00:12:27,890 --> 00:12:29,580
Want to take a look?

143
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:43,570
<i>Please leave your message after the tone.</i>

144
00:12:45,150 --> 00:12:50,060
Yui. The police told me Mari is safe.

145
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,910
Tell me what's going on.

146
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,520
<i>Hello?</i>

147
00:13:16,230 --> 00:13:19,100
My name is Nanase.
I worked at Professor Ishimizaki's lab.

148
00:13:19,100 --> 00:13:22,060
Is this the home of the Professor's brother?

149
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:24,230
<i>Did you need something from my husband?</i>

150
00:13:24,230 --> 00:13:27,750
No. I wish to speak to Yui, if she is home.

151
00:13:32,980 --> 00:13:34,830
Yes?

152
00:13:35,810 --> 00:13:41,380
I apologize if I seem suspicious.
Yui and I met at the Professor's funeral.

153
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:46,040
That is not funny.

154
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:51,660
My daughter passed away
six years ago in an accident.

155
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:56,430
Please do not bother us again.

156
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:02,210
What?

157
00:14:12,850 --> 00:14:15,150
[Haruka]

158
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:04,400
Shiharu...

159
00:15:31,330 --> 00:15:34,100
We're heading out, Tada.

160
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:38,940
HQ won't share their intel with us, huh?

161
00:15:38,940 --> 00:15:41,040
Then let's get the jump on them.

162
00:15:41,650 --> 00:15:42,830
What?

163
00:15:42,830 --> 00:15:45,180
We have one lead over HQ.

164
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:49,750
I saw the face of this "Ushio". No one else.

165
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:52,700
Come on.

166
00:15:56,690 --> 00:16:01,930
Have Xin Ming Ah been assertive
about buying us out?

167
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:06,600
Not at the moment.
But we cannot let our guard down.

168
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:10,040
I will continue to erase
any remains of "log.0".

169
00:16:12,820 --> 00:16:15,770
Are there any concerns regarding the Plantae?

170
00:16:15,770 --> 00:16:18,100
I know they've been sending out Ushio.

171
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:21,540
- If your family...
- That is none of your concern.

172
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:24,700
My apologies, sir.

173
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:32,350
I appreciate you looking out for my son.

174
00:16:32,350 --> 00:16:35,200
I'm sorry to make you juggle so much.

175
00:16:37,270 --> 00:16:40,410
I'm just glad he is alive and well.

176
00:16:41,520 --> 00:16:42,940
Indeed.

177
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:51,160
I think the experience was necessary
for him to grow up, sir.

178
00:17:08,650 --> 00:17:11,180
I reckon the hydrangeas will bloom soon.

179
00:17:12,690 --> 00:17:17,160
You know, I finally saw
Haruka smile yesterday.

180
00:17:22,990 --> 00:17:27,250
We made the right choice.

181
00:18:27,270 --> 00:18:29,540
Happy birthday.

182
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:36,170
Thank you.

183
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:45,950
Do I add all this sugar?

184
00:18:45,950 --> 00:18:48,590
Add as much as you want. It's your birthday.

185
00:18:48,590 --> 00:18:51,000
Then all in it goes.

186
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:57,520
Hey, look. Twins.

187
00:18:57,520 --> 00:18:59,330
Woah, that's rare.

188
00:19:00,690 --> 00:19:02,950
I wonder which one's the real chick.

189
00:19:02,950 --> 00:19:05,970
Huh? They both are.

190
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:09,100
- Right.
- The yolks are right there.

191
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:10,580
Fair point.

192
00:19:10,580 --> 00:19:13,950
<i>Shiharu, should I really be whisking by hand?</i>

193
00:19:13,950 --> 00:19:16,000
<i>It feels like I'll be whisking forever.</i>

194
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,870
No.

195
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:12,250
No.

196
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,420
No.

197
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:17,900
No.

198
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:19,240
No.

199
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:20,800
No.

200
00:20:23,700 --> 00:20:25,330
No.

201
00:20:25,330 --> 00:20:27,690
Shiharu was here.

202
00:20:27,690 --> 00:20:29,830
She was right here.

203
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:35,050
Shiharu was here.

204
00:20:36,070 --> 00:20:37,820
Her clothes.

205
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,870
Her clothes.

206
00:20:39,870 --> 00:20:41,620
Shiharu's...

207
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:48,480
Why?

208
00:20:51,590 --> 00:20:53,560
Why?

209
00:21:14,770 --> 00:21:16,680
Stop.

210
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:22,120
Stop.

211
00:21:24,770 --> 00:21:26,620
Stop it.

212
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,100
Stop.

213
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:48,200
Stop!

214
00:21:56,940 --> 00:21:58,800
I need to ask a favor.

215
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:03,520
You've been looking into
Kyoichi Nanase, I assume?

216
00:22:03,520 --> 00:22:05,180
Yes.

217
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:07,060
<i>And his family, too?</i>

218
00:22:07,060 --> 00:22:08,520
But of course.

219
00:22:08,520 --> 00:22:12,810
<i>I want information,
specifically about his son.</i>

220
00:22:12,810 --> 00:22:14,270
Do you have a lead?

221
00:22:14,270 --> 00:22:16,900
That's what I want to know.

222
00:22:16,900 --> 00:22:20,450
I bet it ties into all this somehow.

223
00:22:20,450 --> 00:22:23,770
Fine. I'll gather our findings for you.

224
00:22:23,770 --> 00:22:25,940
Where are you right now?

225
00:22:25,940 --> 00:22:29,770
I'm about to infiltrate enemy territory.

226
00:22:29,770 --> 00:22:32,600
<i>Take care not to be eaten alive.</i>

227
00:22:43,690 --> 00:22:47,220
I am Kasuga, the head of PR
for the Plantae Gathering.

228
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:50,610
Excuse me.

229
00:22:50,610 --> 00:22:55,480
I am Hirama, editor-in-chief of Toho Journal.

230
00:22:55,480 --> 00:22:57,600
- Please, have a seat.
- Thank you.

231
00:22:57,600 --> 00:22:59,770
I read through your draft.

232
00:22:59,770 --> 00:23:02,100
Thank you.

233
00:23:02,100 --> 00:23:05,750
Though your organization
is commonly seen as a religious one,

234
00:23:05,750 --> 00:23:09,060
the Plantae Gathering is also a crucial NPO.

235
00:23:09,060 --> 00:23:12,980
I hoped to make such things clear
with this article.

236
00:23:12,980 --> 00:23:15,850
If that sounds alright with you?

237
00:23:15,850 --> 00:23:19,030
So long as I get eyes on the final draft.

238
00:23:19,030 --> 00:23:20,980
Of course.

239
00:23:20,980 --> 00:23:26,100
"All who suffer must offer
their flesh and blood

240
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:28,350
to quench thy thirst."

241
00:23:28,350 --> 00:23:33,440
"All sacrifice will one day
return to your body."

242
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:38,660
"Like Plantae, who bear fruit
and flourish in rain."

243
00:23:40,060 --> 00:23:43,790
So are the teachings
of Brother Sojiro Manabe.

244
00:23:45,520 --> 00:23:47,920
Such inspiring words.

245
00:23:49,770 --> 00:23:52,350
I believe we said no photography allowed?

246
00:23:52,350 --> 00:23:56,920
Right, my apologies. Habits are habits.

247
00:23:58,270 --> 00:24:03,750
I feel a real sense of community here

248
00:24:03,750 --> 00:24:07,600
that has been lost in our modern era.

249
00:24:07,600 --> 00:24:10,100
Indeed.

250
00:24:10,100 --> 00:24:15,100
We want our believers
to all help one another.

251
00:24:15,100 --> 00:24:17,690
We do not promote fraudulent scams,

252
00:24:17,690 --> 00:24:23,980
nor generous offerings of any sort.

253
00:24:23,980 --> 00:24:26,920
Fascinating.

254
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:34,980
I am impressed with Mr. Manabe's network.

255
00:24:34,980 --> 00:24:38,570
He knew people in politics, finance -
all over, really.

256
00:24:38,570 --> 00:24:41,770
And you maintain various connections
even after his death?

257
00:24:41,770 --> 00:24:44,600
Yes. We do frequent volunteer work

258
00:24:44,600 --> 00:24:48,980
to engage with people
from many different fields.

259
00:24:48,980 --> 00:24:51,210
I see.

260
00:24:57,410 --> 00:25:02,530
[Sharing memories of "the Land of Souls"]
[Sojiro Manabe x Yumihiko Nanase]

261
00:25:05,060 --> 00:25:08,040
Ms. Kasuga, a moment?

262
00:25:08,040 --> 00:25:10,960
- May I?
- Of course.

263
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:37,090
Excuse me.

264
00:26:15,410 --> 00:26:18,550
[Dear Shiharu]

265
00:26:36,690 --> 00:26:38,940
Thank you for your time today.

266
00:26:38,940 --> 00:26:41,870
Thank you for visiting.

267
00:26:46,290 --> 00:26:49,900
This is a painting by Brother Sojiro Manabe

268
00:26:49,900 --> 00:26:54,980
of a place he visited in India.

269
00:26:54,980 --> 00:26:56,620
India?

270
00:26:59,780 --> 00:27:02,770
"The Land of Souls".

271
00:27:02,770 --> 00:27:07,130
It is said to be a sacred land.

272
00:27:11,350 --> 00:27:15,560
I shall remain in touch.

273
00:27:15,560 --> 00:27:17,020
Please do.

274
00:27:17,020 --> 00:27:18,750
Thank you again for having me.

275
00:27:36,770 --> 00:27:38,660
- Hello.
- Hey there.

276
00:27:38,660 --> 00:27:40,440
Was your infiltration a success?

277
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:42,310
I blended right in.

278
00:27:42,310 --> 00:27:45,560
Here is everything we have
on the Nanase family.

279
00:27:45,560 --> 00:27:47,100
I sent you the digital files as well.

280
00:27:47,100 --> 00:27:49,540
Thank you, thank you.

281
00:27:50,200 --> 00:27:52,070
Let's see here...

282
00:27:56,450 --> 00:27:59,400
So Haruka is his step-son.

283
00:27:59,400 --> 00:28:01,590
This was Kyoichi's first marriage.

284
00:28:02,290 --> 00:28:06,830
And Haruka's mother was named Kaede Tozaki.

285
00:28:09,330 --> 00:28:11,170
Wait a second...

286
00:28:12,480 --> 00:28:14,940
Is she really...

287
00:28:14,940 --> 00:28:17,550
Yes. I'm sure of it.

288
00:28:17,550 --> 00:28:21,670
We hadn't noticed the connection
until now either.

289
00:28:22,340 --> 00:28:25,560
To acquire such intel so easily...

290
00:28:25,560 --> 00:28:30,190
Wish I could boast to the police about it.

291
00:28:30,190 --> 00:28:32,690
We aren't a charity case, understand?

292
00:28:32,690 --> 00:28:35,430
Yeah, I hear you.

293
00:28:36,590 --> 00:28:42,160
I found something tying this case
to Nichie, and the Plantae.

294
00:28:45,570 --> 00:28:47,090
Bones?

295
00:28:47,090 --> 00:28:50,480
It's a place in the Himalayas.

296
00:28:50,480 --> 00:28:52,730
A lake, called Roopkund.

297
00:28:52,730 --> 00:28:56,700
Those at Plantae call it "the Land of Souls".

298
00:28:57,380 --> 00:28:59,080
Souls...

299
00:28:59,700 --> 00:29:05,970
That being said, I still don't have enough
to reach Kyoichi Nanase.

300
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:13,370
The stolen remains from Roopkund, huh?

301
00:29:19,330 --> 00:29:21,620
I can't find anything.

302
00:29:53,060 --> 00:29:58,270
Sorry to scare you!
I'm Hirama, from Toho Journal.

303
00:29:58,270 --> 00:30:03,200
I'm investigating the matters surrounding
Professor Ishimizaki's death.

304
00:30:03,200 --> 00:30:06,790
You must be an acquaintance
of the Professor, yes?

305
00:30:07,400 --> 00:30:13,250
Were you the individual
helping Haruka Nanase search for his sister?

306
00:30:14,060 --> 00:30:17,020
I'd like to speak with you.

307
00:30:17,020 --> 00:30:21,120
I promise, I'm on your side.

308
00:30:23,070 --> 00:30:26,160
Please, if I could just have a moment.

309
00:30:26,940 --> 00:30:29,490
I'd like to hear what you know.

310
00:30:33,570 --> 00:30:37,000
You were ambushed by
a mysterious man, correct?

311
00:30:38,020 --> 00:30:42,810
In looking into the disappearance
of Haruka's sister,

312
00:30:42,810 --> 00:30:47,100
you got too close to the truth
of another mystery.

313
00:30:47,750 --> 00:30:52,910
I received a warning from him as well,
back when I was none the wiser.

314
00:30:52,910 --> 00:30:54,630
You too?

315
00:30:57,320 --> 00:31:03,960
How much do you and Haruka know

316
00:31:04,640 --> 00:31:06,620
of the Plantae Gathering?

317
00:31:08,190 --> 00:31:10,190
Plantae?

318
00:31:10,190 --> 00:31:11,660
Yes.

319
00:31:12,270 --> 00:31:14,250
What are you talking about?

320
00:31:16,440 --> 00:31:17,780
You don't know?

321
00:31:17,780 --> 00:31:20,200
Is there a lead there?

322
00:31:20,940 --> 00:31:24,040
Haruka didn't tell you about them?

323
00:31:26,810 --> 00:31:31,670
We were looking into an individual
named Kayoko Senba.

324
00:31:31,670 --> 00:31:34,010
The developmental biologist.

325
00:31:34,570 --> 00:31:37,870
A biologist.

326
00:31:38,770 --> 00:31:42,810
Then she knew Professor Ishimizaki?

327
00:31:42,810 --> 00:31:48,060
They were both a part
of the same research team 27 years ago.

328
00:31:48,060 --> 00:31:51,000
Were they doing research at Roopkund?

329
00:31:52,150 --> 00:31:56,170
I knew something was up with that lake.

330
00:31:56,990 --> 00:32:01,150
Haruka's father was a part
of the research team as well.

331
00:32:01,150 --> 00:32:02,810
Kyoichi Nanase?

332
00:32:02,810 --> 00:32:06,800
What happened at Roopkund? Please, tell me.

333
00:32:08,940 --> 00:32:11,480
I'm still not certain.

334
00:32:11,480 --> 00:32:13,580
But this I can say for sure.

335
00:32:14,330 --> 00:32:18,370
You shouldn't get involved any further.

336
00:32:18,370 --> 00:32:20,830
This case is a dangerous one.

337
00:32:21,650 --> 00:32:24,670
Mrs. Senba told us the same thing.

338
00:32:26,690 --> 00:32:28,600
I see.

339
00:32:28,600 --> 00:32:32,920
That "Senba" gave you good advice.

340
00:32:34,740 --> 00:32:37,310
Would it help to ask Nanase about all this?

341
00:32:37,310 --> 00:32:38,980
Kyoichi Nanase, I mean.

342
00:32:38,980 --> 00:32:41,100
Well, now.

343
00:32:41,100 --> 00:32:43,380
You can't just book a meeting with him.

344
00:32:43,380 --> 00:32:46,160
I have someone I'm looking for.

345
00:32:50,190 --> 00:32:53,450
I've already lost a friend

346
00:32:53,450 --> 00:32:57,630
who had gotten too involved in this case.

347
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:04,310
Remember, I'm with Toho Journal.

348
00:33:04,310 --> 00:33:08,250
I promise to report a big scoop for you.

349
00:33:12,070 --> 00:33:13,510
<i>She exists.</i>

350
00:33:15,020 --> 00:33:16,960
<i>Shiharu exists.</i>

351
00:33:19,600 --> 00:33:22,050
<i>She'll come back.</i>

352
00:34:04,940 --> 00:34:08,470
[Dear Shiharu]

353
00:34:15,020 --> 00:34:16,810
Shiharu exists.

354
00:34:22,980 --> 00:34:24,630
Shiharu...

355
00:34:26,350 --> 00:34:29,000
<i>She exists.</i>

356
00:35:18,850 --> 00:35:20,620
I'm sorry, Shiharu.

357
00:35:40,740 --> 00:35:42,330
What the...

358
00:35:43,310 --> 00:35:49,030
[Giving birth to you, was my greatest gift.]
[Kaede]

359
00:35:52,200 --> 00:35:54,000
Mom...

360
00:35:57,020 --> 00:35:59,130
Mom gave birth to Shiharu?

361
00:36:52,460 --> 00:36:55,140
Kei.

362
00:36:55,140 --> 00:36:56,600
Want some ice cream?

363
00:36:56,600 --> 00:36:58,380
- Really?
- Of course.

364
00:36:58,380 --> 00:37:00,580
Yay!

365
00:37:06,560 --> 00:37:10,690
<i>You are my accomplice.</i>

366
00:37:13,780 --> 00:37:17,120
I wonder who could be visiting at this hour?

367
00:37:22,100 --> 00:37:23,670
Hello?

368
00:37:28,870 --> 00:37:32,790
Yes, she's home. May I get a name?

369
00:37:35,440 --> 00:37:38,900
Yes, I'm safe.

370
00:37:38,900 --> 00:37:40,700
Thank you for letting me escape.

371
00:37:40,700 --> 00:37:43,440
<i>Of course! It was fun for me, too.</i>

372
00:37:43,440 --> 00:37:47,200
But my mother-in-law
gave those poor officers hell.

373
00:37:47,200 --> 00:37:51,440
It's like she has to look down on everyone.

374
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:55,230
<i>So? Have you figured out
my mother-in-law's secret?</i>

375
00:37:55,230 --> 00:37:57,440
Not yet. I'll need a bit more time.

376
00:37:57,440 --> 00:37:59,100
I see.

377
00:37:59,100 --> 00:38:04,150
She's been on edge since you escaped,
so I thought something happened.

378
00:38:04,150 --> 00:38:09,290
She usually keeps
her emotions in check, you know?

379
00:38:09,290 --> 00:38:13,400
<i>Maybe that's why
she's attached to my son these days.</i>

380
00:38:13,400 --> 00:38:15,570
<i>It's seriously annoying.</i>

381
00:38:15,570 --> 00:38:17,080
Where is she now?

382
00:38:17,080 --> 00:38:22,150
She's in her room entertaining a guest.

383
00:38:22,150 --> 00:38:26,150
<i>I can't believe anyone would visit so late.</i>

384
00:38:33,450 --> 00:38:37,100
Welcome home, Haruka Nanase.

385
00:38:37,100 --> 00:38:38,870
I've been waiting for you.

386
00:38:38,870 --> 00:38:42,210
I am Hirama, from Toho Journal.

387
00:38:44,270 --> 00:38:48,000
It all began with the bones from Roopkund.

388
00:38:52,580 --> 00:38:54,330
Isn't that right?

389
00:38:59,810 --> 00:39:03,690
Everything began 27 years ago,
during a particular research expedition.

390
00:39:03,690 --> 00:39:08,000
An expedition your step-father
also participated in.

391
00:39:08,690 --> 00:39:11,330
This all ties back
to the previous Nichie head.

392
00:39:12,890 --> 00:39:20,340
<i>I think Nichie Pharmaceutical
funded that entire expedition.</i>

393
00:39:21,240 --> 00:39:26,810
And now, they're trying to cover it up.

394
00:39:26,810 --> 00:39:30,000
Why come to me about this?

395
00:39:30,480 --> 00:39:35,310
You're not so innocent, are you?

396
00:39:35,310 --> 00:39:37,480
<i>Professor Ishimizaki,
who was a part of the team,</i>

397
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:41,270
<i>and asked you to analyze
those Roopkund remains,</i>

398
00:39:41,270 --> 00:39:44,450
<i>was murdered.</i>

399
00:39:45,080 --> 00:39:48,420
<i>You yourself were assaulted</i>

400
00:39:48,420 --> 00:39:54,000
<i>for looking into Kayoko Senba,
another member of the team.</i>

401
00:39:57,900 --> 00:40:00,710
What exactly is at Roopkund?

402
00:40:01,550 --> 00:40:04,810
That's what I want to know.

403
00:40:04,810 --> 00:40:06,440
You aren't fooling me.

404
00:40:06,440 --> 00:40:09,340
What do you think I know?

405
00:40:10,770 --> 00:40:16,840
Your mother passed away seven years ago, yes?

406
00:40:18,900 --> 00:40:24,160
My guess is that her death
is tied to all this as well.

407
00:40:27,650 --> 00:40:32,690
Those in Plantae call Roopkund,
"the Land of Souls".

408
00:40:32,690 --> 00:40:35,420
They worship the place.

409
00:40:38,350 --> 00:40:41,200
What's so special about that lake?

410
00:40:41,990 --> 00:40:45,630
You'd know, wouldn't you?

411
00:40:46,560 --> 00:40:51,220
As a former Plantae worshipper.

412
00:40:57,270 --> 00:41:00,220
My mother was the religious one.

413
00:41:02,100 --> 00:41:07,460
"All who suffer must offer
their flesh and blood

414
00:41:07,460 --> 00:41:09,850
to quench thy thirst."

415
00:41:09,850 --> 00:41:14,480
"All sacrifice will one day
return to your body."

416
00:41:14,480 --> 00:41:17,500
"Like Plantae, who bear fruit
and flourish in rain."

417
00:41:17,500 --> 00:41:20,160
Please leave.

418
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:27,980
"Like Plantae, who bear fruit
and flourish in rain."

419
00:41:27,980 --> 00:41:32,410
"Rain does not choose the dry.
It supplies to all."

420
00:41:42,230 --> 00:41:46,650
"Water climbs the heavens,
till it returns to Earth."

421
00:41:56,280 --> 00:41:58,530
Forgive them.

422
00:42:01,610 --> 00:42:03,510
Everything will be okay.

423
00:42:05,690 --> 00:42:09,540
All manners occur in an eternal cycle.

424
00:42:13,500 --> 00:42:17,690
<i>Are the Plantae involved
in everything that's going on?</i>

425
00:42:17,690 --> 00:42:20,430
Yeah. I'm sure of it.

426
00:42:25,070 --> 00:42:27,130
You really don't know anything?

427
00:42:29,400 --> 00:42:32,440
Even though both founders have died,

428
00:42:32,440 --> 00:42:36,750
the tie between Nichie and Plantae remains.

429
00:42:39,980 --> 00:42:43,010
You should be close to the truth.

430
00:42:45,210 --> 00:42:47,220
Isn't there anything you've realized?

431
00:42:48,080 --> 00:42:53,510
Some secret they wouldn't mind
killing a man to keep.

432
00:43:08,400 --> 00:43:10,160
Please.

433
00:43:11,020 --> 00:43:14,790
Please set me free.

434
00:43:18,960 --> 00:43:22,660
Roopkund, also known as the Land of Souls.

435
00:43:24,100 --> 00:43:26,500
But to me?

436
00:43:28,600 --> 00:43:31,000
It's become nothing more than a cursed lake.

437
00:43:36,230 --> 00:43:38,160
Have you caught on to something?

438
00:43:38,820 --> 00:43:43,370
Kayoko Senba is a developmental biologist.

439
00:43:43,950 --> 00:43:45,580
And what of it?

440
00:43:46,940 --> 00:43:49,550
No, I see now.

441
00:43:50,330 --> 00:43:54,060
You were ambushed
for looking into Kayoko Senba.

442
00:43:54,060 --> 00:43:59,950
She's at the center of it all.

443
00:44:14,830 --> 00:44:16,310
Woah there.

444
00:44:19,810 --> 00:44:22,160
You okay?

445
00:44:43,740 --> 00:44:48,010
Excuse me. I'd like to see President Nanase.

446
00:44:49,650 --> 00:44:51,310
Sir.

447
00:44:51,310 --> 00:44:54,280
I have news regarding the funding of "log.0".

448
00:44:54,280 --> 00:44:56,150
Change of plans. We'll talk later.

449
00:44:56,150 --> 00:44:59,400
- But sir, the funds...
- Later.

450
00:44:59,400 --> 00:45:01,160
Now leave me.

451
00:45:01,830 --> 00:45:03,430
Yes, sir.

452
00:45:27,490 --> 00:45:29,120
Then if you'll excuse me.

453
00:45:34,030 --> 00:45:35,660
Welcome.

454
00:45:43,410 --> 00:45:46,120
I am Ishimizaki's daughter, Mari.

455
00:45:47,190 --> 00:45:50,100
I came to ask about Shiharu Nanase.
